{
  "raw": {
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4561483": {
      "title": "Staff Clinical Coordinator, Graduate Nursing Programs",
      "description": "Staff Clinical Coordinator, Graduate Nursing Programs. Keuka College. Description Summary: Keuka College invites applications for a regular part-time (20 hours a week) Clinical Coordinator. This position provides operational leadership and coordination of clinical education experiences for graduate nursing programs. Reporting to the Executive Director of the Division of Nursing, the Clinical Coordinator serves as the primary liaison between the College and clinical partners, ensuring high-quality clinical learning experiences that support student success and meet program outcomes, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements. The Clinical Coordinator plans, coordinates, facilitates, administers, and evaluates clinical education activities in collaboration with faculty, students, healthcare agencies, and community partners. Responsibilities include clinical placement management, healthcare partnership development, student and faculty compliance oversight, clinical scheduling, accreditation support, and continuous quality improvement initiatives in compliance with the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) and New York State Department of Education (NYSED) standards. This is a staff position, with the opportunity to teach at the College based on qualifications. Key Responsibilities: Clinical Placement and Partnership Management Coordinate and secure clinical placements for students in graduate nursing programs. Develop and maintain clinical schedules in collaboration with faculty and healthcare partners. Identify, develop, and maintain relationships with healthcare agencies, preceptors, and community partners. Facilitate the acquisition, maintenance, and renewal of clinical affiliation agreements. Maintain databases of agency contacts, placement requests, confirmations, and clinical requirements. Coordinate site visits and represent the College at clinical partner and professional meetings as appropriate. Student Compliance and Clinical Readiness Monitor student compliance with agency requirements, including health records, certifications, background checks, drug screenings, and other required documentation. Coordinate student onboarding and orientation requirements for clinical agencies. Maintain accurate and secure clinical placement and compliance records. Collaborate with faculty and staff to ensure students meet all clinical readiness requirements. Faculty and Program Support Collaborate with nursing leadership and faculty to determine clinical placement needs based on curriculum and enrollment. Assist with onboarding and support of clinical instructors, adjunct faculty, and preceptors. Maintain records of faculty compliance with agency-specific requirements. Serve as a resource for faculty, students, and clinical partners regarding clinical policies, procedures, and placement requirements. Assist in resolving clinical placement, scheduling, and compliance issues. Assessment, Accreditation, and Quality Improvement Support the development, implementation, and evaluation of the clinical education component of the nursing curriculum. Assist with data collection, reporting, and documentation for program assessment, accreditation, and regulatory compliance. Support compliance with CCNE standards, New York State regulations, and clinical agency requirements. Participate in continuous quality improvement initiatives related to clinical education, student learning outcomes, and clinical site effectiveness. Collaborate with nursing leadership to assess and enhance the quality of clinical learning experiences. Requirements Required Qualifications Bachelor of Science in Nursing from an accredited institution required; Master of Science in Nursing preferred. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in New York State or eligibility for New York State licensure. Minimum of three years of clinical nursing experience. Demonstrated knowledge of clinical education, including the planning, coordination, implementation, and evaluation of student clinical learning experiences. Knowledge of healthcare regulations, accreditation standards, clinical agency requirements, and student compliance processes necessary to support safe, effective, and compliant clinical education experiences. Understanding of nursing practice, healthcare systems, and clinical education processes. Experience coordinating with clinical agencies, faculty, preceptors, and students to support clinical placements and learning opportunities. Strong organizational, communication, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, healthcare agencies, and community partners. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, database management systems, electronic record-keeping platforms, and clinical placement software. Ability to manage multiple priorities, complex schedules, and competing deadlines while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Strong problem-solving, leadership, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise sound professional judgment, and uphold professional and ethical standards. Demonstrated commitment to student success, professional nursing standards, diversity and inclusion, and continuous quality improvement. Experience working with accreditation standards and regulatory requirements related to nursing education. Experience developing and maintaining partnerships with healthcare organizations and clinical agencies. Teaching or faculty experience in nursing education preferred. Employee Benefits Overview Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community: Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4561179": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Nursing",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Nursing. Keuka College. Description Summary: Administrative Assistants in Academic Affairs are responsible for supporting their assigned Division Chair/Executive Director and faculty by managing the administrative aspects of academic programs and assisting with communication to all stakeholders. The required performance standards for this position include professionalism, confidentiality, accuracy and timeliness in project completion, excellent customer service, and College values aligned work. While Academic Affairs Administrative Assistants are assigned to an academic division, they also provide cross-divisional assistance when needed. The Administrative Assistant assists in day-to-day academic operations and will perform a wide variety of duties, including administrative and clerical functions, in support of student learning and ensuring academic accreditation standards are met. The Administrative Assistant is responsible for answering programmatic and divisional questions from prospective students/families, demonstrating excellent communication skills (i.e., written, verbal, and interpersonal), and providing a positive experience for students and their families, faculty, and staff of Keuka College. Essential Responsibilities: Program Administrative Support Manage daily operations, annual project workflows, and calendar of activities in the division. Manage and assist the Chair/Executive Director with division budget. Collaborate with the Chair/Executive Director to support the implementation of short and long-range goals, objectives, and operating procedures consistent with the College’s strategic plan, policies, and procedures. Assist the Chair/Executive Director with scheduling and other functions related to the Office of Records and Registration. Assist the Chair/Executive Director in the semesterly syllabi collection, review, and sharing to the Provost’s Office. Assist the Chair/Executive Director in ensuring the effective and optimized use of College technologies. Collect and maintain experiential records and graduate records as needed by the academic program(s). Integrate students and faculty into College technological information services. Manage and assist the Chair/Executive Director in the planning and delivery of instructor workshops, meetings, and program activities. Coordinate and manage new faculty hiring process, onboarding, and orientation. Assist the Chair/Executive Director with the faculty evaluation process as needed. Manage and assist in the hiring, scheduling, coordinating, payroll tracking, supervision, and evaluation of student employees working in various capacities for division programs. Attend division and College meetings to support effectiveness and assessment, and provide administrative support for these meetings. Assist with the creation of program materials with attention to detail, accuracy, and timeliness; maintain materials related to College and/or academic program accreditation and program evaluation related to compliance tasks in a highly organized manner. Serve as a resource to all stakeholders through proactive problem solving. Responsible for ensuring that assigned tasks are completed in compliance with various institutional regulatory requirements, including all accreditation standards. Meet other program needs as directed by the Chair/Executive Director. Communication Maintain current knowledge of College and divisional information. Responsible for initial contact with all visitors and requests for information to the division and serves as the liaison between the division, campus offices, and experiential ed placement sites. Manage and direct student issues to the appropriate parties based on College policies and procedures. Serve as the first point of contact for Facilities, Office of Records and Registration, IT, Client & Conference Services, and the Bookstore. Serve as the person of contact for prospective and current adjunct faculty. Maintain and facilitate communication with students, faculty, staff, and external constituents through all modes of delivery for the academic program(s) within and beyond the division. Promote division functions and maintain information. Manage and coordinate the activities in support of feedback regarding curriculum. Assist the Chair/Executive Director with student academic standing review and communication as directed. Assessment Collect and file syllabi, student teaching records, graduate records, and division/department meeting minutes and provide copies as needed. Support the Chair/Executive Director in the management and coordination of activities in support of ongoing curriculum evaluation, review/revision, and updates by compiling necessary information from multiple sources in the preparation of annual assessment reports in consultation with content experts. Coordinates the collection, compilation, analysis, and presentation of program data, and assists the Chair/Executive Director in the development of comprehensive statistical and narrative program reports. Retain records on job placements/graduate school attendance for division graduates. Manage and coordinate the activities to develop and support assessment processes for academic programs. Division-Specific Responsibilities: (AHW) Work collaboratively with Program Director and Academic Fieldwork Coordinator to ensure effective, efficient and organized use and management of the OT fieldwork program's electronic clinical management program. (EDU/PSY) Assist with NYSED and accreditation related compliance tasks. (EDU/PSY) Student Teacher Placement Coordinator Tasks: Locate school districts (local and out of area) and arrange placements for student teachers each semester; Collect & review student resumes for distribution to districts; Organize & distribute student teaching materials to supervisors, cooperating teachers, local school district administrators and student teachers; Maintain positive interface with school districts; Maintain records & files for all student teachers; Prepare and maintain MOUs; Communicate with student teachers before and during student teaching when needed. (HFA) Manage and coordinate activities necessary to provide American Sign Language interpreters for all College needs, including booking, invoicing, and processing of funds transfers; maintenance of the ASL Lab; managing paperwork related to student internships. (HFA) Promote Humanities & Fine Arts events and activities such as gallery exhibits, student workshops, band and chorale performances through setup, internal photos, flyers, emails, announcements, file maintenance, and interactions with other areas of the college, as appropriate. (NUR) Assist the undergraduate and graduate clinical coordinator(s) with the collection of program materials, including but not limited to affiliation agreements, student clinical readiness and logged hours documentation, clinical faculty and preceptor documentation, student and site evaluation records. (NUR) Assist Executive Director of Nursing, Nursing Program Directors, and Nursing faculty with accreditation and re-accreditation processes. Assist program with the procurement and distribution of evaluation tools and management of division records required by CCNE and NYSED. Coordinate with Executive Director, Program Directors, and CCNE and/or NYSED OPP in preparation for site visits. (SWK) Assist the BSW and MSW Field Directors and Clinical Field Director with the collection of program evaluation materials, including but not limited to, informed consents, surveys. (SWK) Assist Program Directors/Chair and respective faculty, both BSW and MSW, with accreditation and re-accreditation processes. Coordinate with Program Directors, Division Chair and Commissioner in preparation for site visits. (SWK) Assist program Field Office with the procurement and distribution of evaluation tools. Coordinate and track the distribution and processing of field related documentation. Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Two to three years of experience in an Administrative Assistant, Office Manager, or equivalent position required. Experience in a higher education setting is preferred. High School diploma or GED required; Associates degree preferred. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Proficiency in software packages (e.g., M365, Slate, Moodle, WebAdvisor, Handshake, Exxat, Inplace, Typhon), ethical artificial intelligence usage, and office equipment used by the College and/or an indication of the ability to develop proficiency based on transferable computing skills. Ability to effectively communicate both verbally and in writing, with an excellent service disposition is required. Ability to meet regulators, accreditors, and College standards with efficiency and accuracy. Behaviors aligned with a high level of integrity and complete confidentiality. Excellent planning and organizational skills with the ability to work independently in support of the College’s strategic plan goals and student learning outcomes. Sensitivity to and responsiveness to needs/concerns of students, faculty, staff, and the public. Ability to work under pressure with a high tolerance for interruptions and to work with diverse groups of people. Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Some evening and weekend hours are required. Occasional lifting, pushing, and pulling of up to 25 pounds. Employee Benefits Overview Comprehensive Medical, Dental and Vision Coverage Financial assistance for educational expenses, enabling professional growth and development. Protection for you and your loved ones with employer-sponsored life insurance coverage. Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community: Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4293538": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing. Keuka College. Description Position Summary Keuka College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing. Rank is commensurate with qualifications and experience. This role offers an opportunity to prepare the next generation of highly competent, compassionate, and practice-ready nurses through innovative, student-centered education. The successful candidate will teach across undergraduate and graduate programs in both on-campus and online modalities. We are seeking a dynamic nurse educator with clinical expertise in mental health nursing, strong teaching skills, a commitment to student success, academic excellence, and inclusive learning environments. Key Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate nursing courses (didactic and/or clinical) in face-to-face, hybrid and asynchronous online formats. Develop, implement, and evaluate course content aligned with student learning outcomes, AACN competencies, and current nursing practice standards. Design and assess student learning using evidence-based teaching and evaluation strategies. Provide timely feedback and maintain accurate records of student performance, progression, and outcomes. Foster an inclusive, engaging learning environment that promotes clinical judgment, critical thinking, and professional development. Advise and mentor students, supporting academic progression, licensure readiness, and career development. Participate in curriculum development, revision, and continuous quality improvement initiatives. Contribute to program assessment, outcomes evaluation, and continuous improvement processes. Support accreditation and regulatory compliance through documentation, reporting, and data-driven decision-making. Engage in shared governance, including active participation on departmental, divisional, and college-wide committees. Collaborate on student recruitment, retention, and program growth initiatives. Maintain an active role in service and, as appropriate, scholarship and professional development. Demonstrate professionalism, ethical practice, and commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Requirements Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited program. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license or eligibility for licensure in New York State. Recent clinical nursing experience. Demonstrated or potential ability to teach in higher education. Knowledge of nursing education standards, student learning outcomes, and clinical evaluation. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to teach in both in-person and online environments (experience with LMS platforms preferred). Commitment to student-centered teaching, mentoring, and inclusive excellence. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Nursing (PhD, EdD, DNP) or related field. One of the two highest degrees must be in nursing. Prior teaching experience in undergraduate and/or graduate nursing programs. Experience with online teaching, simulation, or clinical instruction. Familiarity with accreditation, regulatory standards, and outcomes assessment in nursing education. Experience with curriculum design, program evaluation, and quality improvement. Engagement in scholarship, research, or professional practice. Physical Requirements Occasional lifting of boxes, supplies, etc., generally less than 30 lbs. Some evening and weekend hours may be required. Application Materials Required To be considered for this position, applicants must submit the following: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Transcripts demonstrating completion of a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) Copy of a current, unencumbered New York State Registered Professional Nurse (RN) license Copies of all applicable professional certifications, including: Current CPR Certification Any additional nursing related certifications held Incomplete application materials may delay or prevent consideration for this position. Employee Benefits Overview Comprehensive Medical, Dental and Vision Coverage Financial assistance for educational expenses, enabling professional growth and development. Protection for you and your loved ones with employer-sponsored life insurance coverage. Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community: Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4521069": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Childhood Education",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Childhood Education. Keuka College. Description Summary: We invite applications for on-campus full-time tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Childhood Education in Keuka College’s Association for Advancing Quality in Educator Preparation (AAQEP) accredited education program. Rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. This role offers an opportunity to prepare the next generation of highly competent, compassionate, and practice-ready educators through innovative, student-centered approach. The successful candidate will enjoy teaching elementary education and other education courses to education majors preparing for certifications at all levels (early childhood, childhood, adolescent), as well as courses. In addition, the successful candidate will instruct within the College’s the general education “Compass Curriculum” to non-education majors. We are seeking a dynamic educator with strong teaching skills, a commitment to student success and academic excellence, and the ability to create inclusive learning environments. Preference will be given to applicants who in addition to traditional instructional designs can demonstrate knowledge of and demonstrated ability to develop and deliver highly engaging and rigorous content in fully online, hybrid, executive, and/or low residency modalities. Essential Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate in elementary and literacy education and other related education courses to education majors using a variety of delivery formats, including traditional, hybrid, and online. Teach undergraduate courses in the general education curriculum when required using a variety of delivery formats, including traditional, hybrid, and online. Foster an inclusive, engaging learning environment that promotes professional judgment, critical thinking, and pre-service teacher development. Design and assess student learning using evidence-based teaching and evaluation strategies. Provide timely feedback and maintain accurate records of student performance, progression, and outcomes. Advise and mentor students, supporting academic progression, licensure readiness, and career development. Engage students in research projects and/or other scholarly endeavors. Participate in the development, multiple modality implementation, and evaluation/assessment of course content and curriculum aligned with student learning outcomes, AAQEP Standards, and current New York State standards and certification expectations. Support accreditation and regulatory compliance through documentation, reporting, and data-driven decision-making. Engage in shared governance, including active participation on departmental, divisional, and college-wide committees. Collaborate on student recruitment, retention, and program growth initiatives. Maintain an active role in service and, as appropriate, scholarship and professional development. Demonstrate professionalism, ethical practice, and alignment with the College’s mission, vision, and values. Consistently demonstrate high standards of integrity by supporting the Keuka College mission, vision and values and adhering to institutional policies. Maintain student privacy in accordance with the FERPA privacy policies and procedures. Regular and reliable on-campus attendance is expected and required. Requirements Required Qualifications : A graduate degree in elementary education, literacy, or a closely related field from an accredited institution is required. Applicants are expected to have a background in elementary classroom teaching experience, literacy education and teacher preparation instruction leading to childhood Grades 1-6 and/or literacy certification area. State-issued teaching certification in childhood, and/or early childhood, and/or literacy. Demonstrated ability for excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, including the ability to develop and deliver highly engaging and rigorous content in traditional, hybrid, and online modalities. A proven track record of student-centered teaching. Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Ability to teach in both in-person and online environments (experience with LMS platforms preferred). Commitment to student-centered teaching, mentoring, and inclusive excellence. Understand and behave with a high level of integrity and confidentiality at all times. Preferred Qualifications : Doctorate in elementary education, literacy, or a closely related field. Student teacher supervision experience. Prior teaching experience in undergraduate and/or graduate education programs. Experience with online teaching. Familiarity with accreditation, regulatory standards, and outcomes assessment in NYS teacher education. Experience with curriculum design, program evaluation, and quality improvement. Engagement in scholarship and research. Physical Requirements: Some evening and weekend hours required. Occasional lifting of boxes, supplies, etc., generally less than 30 lbs. Application Materials Letter of application (outlining interest in the position, qualifications, experience, and approach to teaching at a liberal arts college) Current Curriculum Vitae Outline of research interests suitable for collaboration with colleagues and students Names and titles of three current professional references with telephone numbers and email contact information (Candidates who are determined to potentially be a good fit with the position will be asked to have these individuals send letters to us.) Transcripts of all academic work (unofficial copies acceptable during application reviews; official copies will be required at the time of hire.) Other supporting information you may choose to provide. Applications must be submitted electronically through the College’s employment application link. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Employee Benefits Overview Comprehensive Medical, Dental and Vision Coverage Financial assistance for educational expenses, enabling professional growth and development. Protection for you and your loved ones with employer-sponsored life insurance coverage. Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. For Education positions: Keuka College’s Education programs prepare future educators through a strong liberal arts foundation, experiential learning, and supportive, technology-enhanced classrooms. The College offers undergraduate pathways in inclusive education leading to New York State teacher certification, as well as Educational Studies and graduate-level programs, including Literacy. Faculty are committed to preparing reflective, collaborative educators who can meet the needs of diverse learners. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community: Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/3941514": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian. Keuka College. Description The custodian will uphold the highest standards of cleanliness and sanitation of the college campus. This role requires meticulous attention to detail, excellent time management skills, and the ability to work effectively as part of a team. You will play a crucial role in creating a clean and welcoming environment for our employees, students, and visitors. Essential Responsibilities: Performs general cleaning and sanitizing tasks and services throughout assigned buildings. Maintains a neat and orderly supply closet; ensures cleaning and maintenance supplies are stocked. Performs general cleaning and sanitizing in bathrooms, kitchens, hallways, classrooms, offices, living spaces and common areas. Performs restorative work to floors such as vacuuming, mopping, buffing, stripping, and waxing. Pick up and empty trash containers. Report any safety or maintenance deficiencies to the lead custodian or facilities manager. Performs other related duties as assigned. Essential Employee Designation: This position has been designated as essential at Keuka College. This means that, in the event of significant incidents or major events, you may be required to be on-site to ensure our operations continue smoothly. Requirements High school diploma or equivalent required. Employment is contingent upon completion of a post-offer background check in compliance with applicable laws. Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods standing. Must be able to lift, bend, stoop, climb, reach, and lift up to 50 pounds at a time. Ability to operate tools or equipment used in routine cleaning. Employee Benefits Overview Comprehensive Medical, Dental and Vision Coverage Financial assistance for educational expenses, enabling professional growth and development. Protection for you and your loved ones with employer-sponsored life insurance coverage. Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/1082891": {
      "title": "Shuttle Driver Pool",
      "description": "Shuttle Driver Pool. Keuka College. Description Summary: The primary responsibility of the shuttle driver will be to transport students to and from destinations for official business, off-campus classes, class trips, and recreation and entertainment opportunities. Drivers will also assist with parking shuttles for special events sponsored by Keuka College. Applications are being accepted for CDL and non-CDL licensed candidates. This is a pool position and candidates will be interviewed on an as-needed basis. Essential Responsibilities: Provide safe and efficient transportation in accordance with Keuka College safety regulations and policies. Maintain valid NY State Class C Driver’s License with Passenger Endorsement and a New York State medical certificate. Responsible for all driving assignments scheduled through Student Affairs. Any driver changes must be coordinated through Student Life. The driver is responsible for the proper completion and handling of paperwork and fuel receipts. Conduct pre and post-inspections of vehicles, clean bus after each trip, and report any mechanical issues to Facilities. Inform passengers of rule infractions such as smoking or inappropriate behavior and the consequences for such behavior. Report any irregularities, such as security breaches, facility and safety hazards, and emergency situations to Campus Safety. In the event of an accident or passenger illness, contact the appropriate emergency agency and cooperate with responders. Responsible for ensuring that assigned tasks are completed in compliance with various institutional and regulatory requirements. Maintain a professional and courteous attitude at all times towards co-workers, and internal and external customers, representing Keuka College, its programs, policies, and procedures in a positive and professional manner. Maintain effective working relationships to ensure institution-wide teamwork. Attend provided/necessary training and other meetings to support effectiveness within the position as required. Consistently demonstrate high standards of integrity by supporting the Keuka College mission, vision, and values and adhering to institutional policies. Maintain a high regard for student privacy in accordance with the FERPA privacy policies and procedures. Regular and reliable attendance is expected and required. Perform other functions as assigned by management. Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Drivers must be a minimum of 18 years of age. This position requires extensive automobile travel throughout the assigned territory; therefore, a valid driver's license and successful DMV check are required. No more than one (1) recordable violation in the past 3 years. Must hold and maintain a valid New York State standard driver's license (Class D); Class C preferred. Ability to effectively communicate both verbally and in writing. Understand and behave with a high level of integrity and complete confidentiality at all times. Ability to be sensitive to and respond to the needs/concerns of students, faculty, college staff, and the public. Ability to work under pressure with a high tolerance for interruptions, and the ability to work with diverse groups of people. Physical Requirements: Driver must be flexible and willing to work weekdays, weekends, and evenings when called upon. Requires ability to sit for extended periods of time, bend, reach, climb stairs, and grasp. Occasional lifting up to 25 lbs. At Keuka, we firmly believe that to live our mission, vision, and values, we need to celebrate our differences. Keuka is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status. In support of the Americans with Disabilities Act, this job description lists only those responsibilities and qualifications deemed essential to the position. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position."
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4467893": {
      "title": "Purchasing and Risk Specialist",
      "description": "Purchasing and Risk Specialist. Keuka College. Description Summary The Purchasing and Risk Specialist manages institutional purchasing and accounts payable activities and coordinates the College’s insurance programs. The position works with campus departments, vendors, insurance providers, and the Business Office to ensure efficient procurement and payment processes, appropriate insurance coverage, regulatory compliance, and adherence to College policies. Essential Responsibilities Purchasing and Procurement Coordinate purchasing transactions with vendors and campus departments. Research and evaluate suppliers based on cost, quality, service, and delivery; assist with negotiations as needed. Solicit and analyze Requests for Proposals (RFPs) and Requests for Quotes (RFQs) as appropriate. Review and process purchase requisitions and create, distribute, and monitor purchase orders. Maintain purchase order records, monitor outstanding encumbrances, and facilitate special-order and capital purchases. Review vendor contracts and coordinate required approvals. Maintain purchasing policies, procedures, forms, and supporting documentation. Serve as a resource to faculty and staff on purchasing procedu res and requirements. Accounts Payable Administration Review invoices, payment requests, and supporting documentation for accuracy, appropriate coding, and policy compliance; match invoices to purchase orders and receiving records. Process vendor payments, manual checks, credit card transactions, and employee reimbursements. Manage staff Ramp (credit card) accounts and provide guidance on credit card transactions, receipt documentation, expense coding, transaction research, and purchases made on behalf of other departments. Maintain vendor records and W-9 documentation and coordinate annual 1099 reporting with the Business Office Maintain documentation related to prepaid expenses and purchasing decision trees. Serve as a resource for faculty and staff regarding purchasing and accounts payable procedures, coding, budget transfers, and related financial requests. Insurance Oversight and Risk Management Administer and coordinate the College’s institutional insurance programs and renewals, including property, liability, workers’ compensation, cyber, automobile, educator’s legal liability, and other applicable coverage. Serve as the primary contact for Certificates of Insurance and coordinate insurance requirements for vendors, contractors, events, facility users, and third-party providers. Coordinate insurance claim reporting, documentation, and follow-up through resolution. Monitor vendor compliance with contractual insurance requirements. Assist with insurance claim reporting and claim documentation, working with College departments and insurance carriers through claim resolution. Maintain records related to vehicle insurance, registrations, and insurance updates. Provide insurance-related reports and analysis to senior leadership as requested. Identify coverage issues or gaps and communicate recommendations to College leadership and insurance partners. Compliance and Administrative Support Ensure purchasing, accounts payable, and insurance activities comply with College policies, internal controls, audit requirements, IRS regulations, and applicable laws. Assist with internal and external audits by providing requested documentation and reports. Support process improvement initiatives related to procurement, payments, and risk management. Assist the Associate Vice President and Controller and Vice President for Finance & Administration as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements Minimum Qualifications Associate degree required; bachelor's degree preferred in Business Administration, Accounting, Finance, Risk Management, or related field. Three to five years of progressively responsible experience in purchasing, accounts payable, accounting, business operations, insurance administration, or a related field. Experience managing vendor relationships and administrative processes. Strong computer skills, including Microsoft Excel, Word, and enterprise financial systems (Ellucian Colleague or equivalent preferred). Demonstrated ability to analyze and interpret contracts, insurance policies, and business documentation. Knowledge of accounts payable practices, purchasing procedures, and internal controls. Understanding of insurance fundamentals, risk management principles, or policy administration strongly preferred. Ability to research, understand, and implement regulatory and compliance requirements. Excellent organizational and project management skills with strong attention to detail. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Abilityto prioritize multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, Risk Management, or related field. Experience with higher education purchasing and accounts payable operations. Experience coordinating commercial insurance programs, renewals, claims, or broker relationships. Knowledge of contract review and vendor risk management. Professional certifications related to purchasing, accounting, or insurance are desirable. Employee Benefits Overview Comprehensive Medical, Dental and Vision Coverage Financial assistance for educational expenses, enabling professional growth and development. Protection for you and your loved ones with employer-sponsored life insurance coverage. Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community: Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4146731": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Social Work",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of Social Work. Keuka College. Description This position is a full-time, 10 month, hybrid, non-tenure-track, faculty position as a Visiting Assistant Professor of Social Work. This faculty member will be responsible for teaching courses at the undergraduate/graduate levels offered through both the traditional on-campus as well as online programs. The teaching load for this position is 4-4 (BSW)/3-3 (MSW), with the possibility of course releases for leadership responsibilities, such as division chair or program director, depending on program needs and candidate qualifications. We are seeking a highly motivated candidate with clinical experience and expertise, who has exceptional organizational and technological skills, with the ability to operate effectively in a dynamic environment while effectively managing multiple responsibilities and competing priorities. The qualified candidate will support Keuka College through active engagement and service. Keuka College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to a diverse and inclusive workforce. Essential Responsibilities: Teach Social Work courses at the undergraduate/graduate levels for both the traditional on-campus as well as online programs. Serve as an advisor to social work students. Support ongoing curriculum review/revisions and updates. Assist the Program Director and Division Chair in writing the CSWE reaffirmation documents. Contribute to the College and the community. On campus attendance at meetings and ceremonies at the beginning of the Fall semester, and at the end of the Spring semester. Demonstrate active research/scholarly activity in the field of Social Work. Demonstrate commitment to excellence in teaching. Work with the Division Chair and the Program Director in the recruitment and retention of students. Consistently demonstrate high standards of integrity by supporting the Keuka College mission, vision, and values and adhering to institutional policies. Maintain high regard for student privacy in accordance with the FERPA privacy policies and procedures. Always maintain a professional and courteous attitude toward co-workers, internal and external customers. Represent Keuka College, its programs, policies, and procedures in a positive and professional manner. Maintain effective working relationships to ensure institution-wide teamwork. Attend provided/necessary training and other meetings to support effectiveness within the position as required. Regular and reliable attendance is expected and required. Perform other administrative duties as assigned. Requirements Minimum Qualifications: PhD or Doctorate in Social Work (DSW) from a Council on Social Work Education Accredited program. Licensure: Eligibility for or possession of social work licensure in New York is required. Two years post-MSW work experience is required. Demonstrated interest and potential for excellence in teaching. Dedication to pursuit of scholarly interests in collaboration with students. Ability to effectively communicate both verbally and in writing. Always understand and behave with a high level of integrity and complete confidentiality. Ability to be sensitive to and respond to needs/concerns of students, faculty, college staff and the public. Cultural competence: Demonstrated cultural sensitivity and competence in program delivery and staff interactions. Collaborative mindset: Ability to work collaboratively with internal and external stakeholders, including community partners, to enhance program effectiveness. Team player: Capacity to work collaboratively with a multidisciplinary team to provide comprehensive social services. Commitment to professional development: Willingness to stay current with evolving social work practices, program management, and relevant trends. Preferred Qualifications: Program leadership: Proven experience in program development, implementation, and management, with a focus on program evaluation. Strategic planning: Demonstrated ability to create and execute strategic plans to meet program goals and objectives. Budget management: Proficiency in budget development and financial oversight for program initiatives. Supervisory skills: Strong leadership and supervisory skills to guide and support program staff effectively. Policy advocacy: Experience in advocating for policy changes or reforms as needed. Physical Requirements: Occasional lifting of boxes, supplies, etc., generally less than 30 lbs. Some evening and weekend hours required Employee Benefits Overview Comprehensive Medical, Dental and Vision Coverage Financial assistance for educational expenses, enabling professional growth and development. Protection for you and your loved ones with employer-sponsored life insurance coverage. Generous paid time off includes holidays and sick leave to ensure work-life balance. Retirement benefits eligible on the 1st day of employment and matching contributions after 6 months of employment Access to confidential counseling and support services for mental health and personal matters through the Employee Assistance Program Work with Purpose at Keuka College Founded in 1890, Keuka College is a private, liberal arts-based institution located on the shores of Keuka Lake in New York’s Finger Lakes region. Our close-knit lakeside campus fosters collaboration, innovation, and personal growth. Why Keuka College? Mission-Driven: Empowering students to lead, serve, and succeed. Experiential Learning: A hands-on, immersive educational environment. Strong Community: A caring, respectful culture rooted in integrity and leadership. Student-Centered: Dedicated to the success of every student. Professional Growth & Balance: Support for your development and well-being. About the Community: Keuka Park offers scenic lakeside living, outdoor recreation, and access to nearby Penn Yan’s small-town charm—all in the heart of the Finger Lakes. Join us and be part of something truly “small on purpose.”"
    },
    "https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/1083707": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach Pool",
      "description": "Assistant Coach Pool. Keuka College. Description Summary: The Keuka College Department of Athletics and Recreation, part of the Division of Student Life, seeks qualified candidates for the position of Assistant Coach (part-time) in a specific sport. This is a pool posting and applicants will be reviewed only when there is a need to fill a position. This part-time, 10-month position will assist in the organization, implementation, and skill instruction of daily practice, and game-day preparation. Must demonstrate the ability to instruct the student-athletes (team) in all aspects of coaching in the absence of the head coach. $500 – $5,000 seasonal stipend based on sport assignment, scope of responsibilities, season length, and experience. The anticipated annual salary will not exceed $5,000. The selected candidate is expected to adhere to all NCAA, Empire 8, and Keuka College rules and regulations. Special Instructions to Applicant: Please indicate which sport(s) you are interested in coaching in the supplemental questions. This is a pool posting and applicants will only be contacted if there is an opening. Essential Responsibilities: Assist in the organization, implementation, and skill instruction of daily practice, and game-day preparation. Teach and train student-athletes in skills and strategies specific to a particular sport/defense/offense, etc. Evaluate and analyze the gameplay reports of the opposing team; then, instruct the student-athletes on methods of developing strategies to address the opposing team’s game tactics. Assist with recruiting as needed. Instruct the team in all aspects of coaching in the absence of the head coach. Assist in the organization and execution of non-traditional and preseason practices, games, training, and conditioning programs. Responsible for ensuring that assigned tasks are completed in compliance with various institutional and regulatory requirements. Maintain a professional and courteous attitude at all times towards co-workers, and internal and external customers, representing Keuka College, its programs, policies, and procedures in a positive and professional manner. Maintain effective working relationships to ensure institution-wide teamwork. Attend provided/necessary training and other meetings to support effectiveness within the position as required. Consistently demonstrate high standards of integrity by supporting the Keuka College mission, vision, and values and adhering to institutional policies. Maintain a high regard for student privacy in accordance with the FERPA privacy policies and procedures. Regular and reliable attendance is expected and required. Perform other functions as assigned by the head coach. Requirements Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Prior coaching experience preferred. Ability to be sensitive to and respond to the needs and concerns of all constituents of the College including but not limited to students, faculty, college staff, and the public. A commitment to the campus values of diversity and inclusivity. Physical Requirements: Occasional local or regional travel may be required. Evening and weekend hours are required. Occasional lifting up to 25 lbs. At Keuka, we firmly believe that to live our mission, vision, and values, we need to celebrate our differences. Keuka is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity, or Veteran status. In support of the Americans with Disabilities Act, this job description lists only those responsibilities and qualifications deemed essential to the position. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position."
    }
  },
